  "question": {
    "text": "Manganese <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>VI</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;has ability to disproportionate in acidic solution. The difference in oxidation states of two ions it forms in acidic solution is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In acidic solution Mn(VI) become unstable relative to Mn(VII) and Mn(IV)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br />So difference in oxidation state of product ions of Mn is = 3</p>",
